  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#2403\", \"PowerToys#35616\", \"PowerToys#29085\"], \"answer\": \"This feature request has been filed before: choosing which utilities to install in the installer and uninstalling individual modules afterwards. It is not currently available. The past tickets show no plan to implement it. In #25348 the team said nothing was planned, in #2403 they said they had no plans, and in #23867 they said they had no plans to break PowerToys apart. Duplicates such as #35616 were closed in favor of the main tracking issues (#25348 and #3170), so add your +1 and your use case, such as disk size, to those threads instead of opening a new one. Meanwhile, you can disable the utilities you don't use in PowerToys Settings so they don't run. Because PowerToys is open source, you can also compile a custom build with only the modules you want, as the team suggested in #23867.\"}",
